<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jimutavahana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jimutavahana is a legendary Vidyadhara prince of Indian story, famed for his self-sacrifice. In the tale, told in the Kathasaritsagara and in King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>'s 7th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> play Nagananda, he offers himself to the bird Garuda in place of a young serpent, and his compassion moves Garuda to give up eating serpents. The Silahara dynasties claimed descent from him.</p></div>
